1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,100
Your next machine is occupied. Searching for the perfect replacement produces a

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,200
dozen confident answers. Start with what you are trying to preserve. An

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:12,300
exercise name, a muscle label, and a training goal are related, but

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:16,400
they are not interchangeable instructions.

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:21,000
Ask three questions. What role does this exercise serve in the plan?

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,600
Which available option can I perform appropriately? And what changes when I

7
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:30,200
switch? Use the answers to discuss an adaptation. A matching muscle name

8
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,800
alone is not enough to claim two exercises are identical.

9
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:39,100
If your goal involves performing a particular lift, practicing that task matters

10
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,400
to the comparison. If your goal is broader, you may ask a

11
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:47,700
different question. The point is to name the goal before treating an

12
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:52,000
equipment swap as either perfect or useless.

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,800
A review comparing free weights and machines found that strength changes depended

14
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:01,600
in part on the task used to test them. It did not

15
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:06,400
detect a difference in muscle growth in the available comparisons. That finding

16
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:11,200
does not prove every individual exercise swap produces exactly the same result.

17
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:15,500
Those studies compared particular programs and equipment. They did not validate every

18
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:19,800
substitution in a crowded gym, or establish a personal injury-risk prediction. Do

19
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:24,100
not use a broad category result to override pain, an unfamiliar technique,

20
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:28,400
or the purpose of your existing program.

21
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,600
Use the substitution questions card to record the goal, the option, and

22
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:36,800
the tradeoff you still need to resolve. A useful explanation should make

23
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:41,000
the next decision clearer. It should not manufacture certainty that the evidence

24
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,200
cannot provide. Know why. Train better.
